            {
                "entry_id": "8dc6500e-1647-3d8e-983b-411ba2c974ec",
                "word": "JPEG",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8b7e0be8-1e14-4c59-962a-dfe15193b750",
                        "entry_id": "8dc6500e-1647-3d8e-983b-411ba2c974ec",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "JPEGs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ea8ccea3-6524-38ac-8940-899d3a4c369f",
                        "entry_id": "8dc6500e-1647-3d8e-983b-411ba2c974ec",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An image using the JFIF image file format, containing an image compressed using JPEG compression."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5a6dad5-bba3-4576-b5ff-7441099d214e",
                                "sense_id": "ea8ccea3-6524-38ac-8940-899d3a4c369f",
                                "text": "a JPEG of a cat"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7d5ca9e-d10d-4a82-bb81-ae892aef3302",
                                "sense_id": "ea8ccea3-6524-38ac-8940-899d3a4c369f",
                                "text": "I'll send you some JPEGs tomorrow."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e110c50-fe69-4d98-8ebe-04a41b735470",
                                "sense_id": "ea8ccea3-6524-38ac-8940-899d3a4c369f",
                                "text": "It's important to note that you cannot interlace a JPEG. However, a technology has been developed to allow JPEGs to progressively render. This is the progressive JPEG format."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "05d42fe6-d024-4168-93ab-1072fbf6b36d",
                                "sense_id": "ea8ccea3-6524-38ac-8940-899d3a4c369f",
                                "text": "Typically, the art object that gets NFT’d is a digital file — maybe a JPEG image or an MP4 video — that lives on some hard drive, and that looks or sounds precisely the way it would have in the decades before NFTs came along."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af7e2642-d9d8-4b9e-aca9-08827f678a4c",
                                "sense_id": "ea8ccea3-6524-38ac-8940-899d3a4c369f",
                                "text": "Critics of NFTs who don't understand the technology wonder why buyers would pay so much for a JPEG when they could just “right-click save” to their computer and copy the image an arbitrary number of times."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fcfed64f-55ed-4a1a-b365-6172ab8a941f",
                                "sense_id": "ea8ccea3-6524-38ac-8940-899d3a4c369f",
                                "text": "Think of ChatGPT as a blurry JPEG of all the text on the Web."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
